---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — PDF Stowaway Scanner"
  description="Why PDF Stowaway Scanner exists and how it checks PDFs for hidden content without ever uploading your files."
  pathname="/about"
>
  <section class="container max-w-2xl py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">About</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-muted-foreground">
      PDFs can hide content that isn't visible on the page: text painted white on white, layers
      turned off by default, font sizes shrunk to nothing, or instructions tucked in off-page
      coordinates. As more documents get summarized or reviewed by AI tools, this hidden content
      has become a way to slip instructions past a human reader and straight to the model reading
      the file on their behalf.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      PDF Stowaway Scanner checks a PDF for these techniques: invisible render modes, white-on-white
      text, tiny fonts, crop box mismatches (the signal left behind when content is cropped off the
      page), hidden optical content groups, embedded files, JavaScript, and known prompt-injection
      phrasing. Everything runs in your browser using WebAssembly. Your file is never uploaded
      anywhere.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      This is a free, open-source tool. It won't catch everything, and it isn't a substitute for
      careful review, but it surfaces the signals that are easy to miss by eye.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
